Could we cap this loop? I was surprised we need a binary search here (considered a few alternatives but don't have a fully working version) and wondered about `NaN` risk, but that does actually make this condition break.
Digging further with AI pointed to x87 excess precision: a midpoint can compare between the endpoints, then round back to one when stored, leaving the loop with no progress. [GCC describes the relevant behavior](https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-13/porting_to.html#excess-precision).

Bound the existing bisection loop

